  "summary": "The three-part fix (HTTP status guard, zero-sections guard, cache reordering) is correct but needs two refinements to avoid introducing new bugs. The zero-sections guard should be conditional — only suppress zero-section responses when the board currently has content (e.g., `if (newSections.length === 0 && curSections.length > 0) return;`) — otherwise legitimately clearing all features from a board becomes impossible, leaving stale cards frozen on screen indefinitely. The cache assignment should be updated on ALL code paths that successfully process a response (including early-return paths like the zero-sections guard), not just after DOM mutation; otherwise identical consecutive responses will redundantly re-diff because the cache never records the last-seen HTML. With these two adjustments the six coordinated changes (3 per polling function) form a complete, correct fix with no regressions."
